			"Message": "style(Maintain): Normalize shell and TypeScript formatting across scripts\n\nApply shfmt formatting normalization across all Maintain shell scripts — fix case-statement indent depth, standardize redirect spacing (`>/dev/null` → `>/dev/null`), align pipe continuations to end-of-line placement, and normalize `2>&1` spacing. Add blank-line separation between import groups and after block-level declarations (async functions, interfaces) in TypeScript codegen files. Insert missing top-level blank lines in prettier.config.js and tailwind.config.js.\n\nNo functional changes — purely formatting consistency aligned with the project's shfmt and Prettier profiles.",
			"SHA": "fc363dbfb501bc585d5835e9adbe7b51f9d2ad7e"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-12T18:48:36Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				155,
				1
			],
			"Message": "chore(Land): Prune unused Tauri plugin and utility crate deps\n\nRemove 23 tauri-plugin-* crates (autostart, barcode-scanner, biometric, cli, clipboard-manager, deep-link, geolocation, global-shortcut, haptics, http, nfc, notification, opener, os, persisted-scope, positioner, process, shell, single-instance, sql, store, stronghold, updater, upload, websocket, window-state), 4 Tauri tooling crates (bundler, cli, driver, macos-sign), tauri-schema-generator, and 3 utility crates (window-vibrancy, window-shadows, global-hotkey) from Cargo.toml.\n\nThese dependencies were declared but never referenced in any crate under the workspace — the editor only uses dialog, fs, localhost, and log from the plugin set. Removing them reduces workspace resolution overhead, eliminates stale pin maintenance, and makes the actual dependency surface explicit.\n\nBoth the crates.io versions and the local Dependency/Tauri/... path overrides are dropped together for each removed crate.",
			"SHA": "85e4da375ec0828818b32787dfae85b4d9bb0304"
		},
